{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2960","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2960","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2960\",\"parent_revision\":\"db525910f94deb1957b789c2f42fa0aefaef7139\",\"root_revision\":\"030260919e697fba0834fc3b4ed400de625a3e8303d3796aac87185ed5238ef4\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/analyze.md`'s Discovery Gate documents a fast path: if the item already has rich groomed sections \u2014 specifically \\\"acceptance criteria\\\", \\\"expected behavior\\\", and \\\"desired structure\\\" (or \\\"scope\\\" as equivalent), all three non-empty \u2014 a feature-context artifact is synthesized directly from those sections instead of invoking the full `dh:discovery` skill, skipping that investigation step entirely.\\n\\n`swarm.md`'s list of required groomer-produced subsections (Reproducibility, Priority, Impact, Benefits, Expected Behavior, Acceptance Criteria, Files, Resources, Dependencies, Effort) never includes \\\"Desired Structure\\\" or \\\"Scope\\\". The `dh:backlog-item-groomer` agent's own output template (`agents/backlog-item-groomer.md`) does list a \\\"Desired Structure\\\" section as one of many optional/conditional sections it may produce, but nothing in `swarm.md`'s orchestrator-facing required-subsection list asks for it, so in practice a groomed item produced by following `swarm.md` as documented will not have that section \u2014 meaning `analyze.md`'s fast-path precondition (all three sections present and non-empty) can structurally never be satisfied by the documented groom-swarm output. The discovery-skip optimization described in `analyze.md` is effectively dead code as the workflow is currently wired.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 discovered during retrospective sweep of groom-workflow docs while grooming #2953, 2026-08-18\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **analyze.md's discovery-skip fast path requires a \\\"desired structure\\\"/\\\"scope\\\" section that swarm.md's groomer never produces \u2014 unreachable in practice** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0dc9f94ec1d4d3d7d30550ef405950086fa71214ca3a7400971c0ccd8ca5cbfa\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTpBvg\"}"}